cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LucidFace, please cite it as below."
title: "LucidFace: Observation-Locked Restoration of Out-of-Focus Faces in Interview Video"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "LucidFace contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ironmark72/lucidface"
keywords:
  - face restoration
  - video restoration
  - defocus deblurring
  - consistency
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  LucidFace restores out-of-focus faces in interview video under one rule: the restoration may add
  only what the camera could not record. A low-frequency consistency lock pins the restored face to
  the observed frame, a detail-only temporal steadier blends along trustworthy optical flow, a focus
  gate leaves in-focus shots untouched, and an eye-centred QC stage flags and fades out doubtful
  frames. Includes a reproducible benchmark built from public-domain interviews.
